# Most of this repository by weight is the Pico lingware, and the sample WAVs are
# most of the rest. Marking them explicitly means git never applies end-of-line
# conversion to them, whatever the checkout platform's defaults happen to be --
# a corrupted .bin does not fail to load, it just makes the voice wrong.
* text=auto

*.bin binary
*.wav binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.lib binary

# Inno Setup compiles this; keep it in the form the compiler expects.
*.iss text eol=crlf

# The vendored Pico sources under third_party/pico/lib deliberately get the same
# text=auto treatment as everything else, which stores them with LF exactly as
# upstream does. That is what keeps a diff against upstream showing only the
# three changes listed in docs/notes.md, rather than every line of every file.
